# Smart System Diagrams

Each use case below includes a simple block diagram (high-level components) and a flowchart (runtime logic) using Mermaid notation.

## Smart Waste Management System
### Block Diagram
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[Bin Fill Sensors] --> E[Edge Controller]
    E --> W[Wireless Network]
    W --> C[Cloud Analytics]
    C --> D[Operations Dashboard]
    D --> F[Collection Fleet Dispatch]
    F --> R[Route Status]
    R --> C
```

### Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Measure fill level]
    B --> C{Threshold exceeded?}
    C -- No --> D[Update status log]
    D --> B
    C -- Yes --> E[Send alert to cloud]
    E --> F[Schedule pickup]
    F --> G[Notify fleet]
    G --> H[Confirm collection]
    H --> B
```

## Smart Water Level Monitoring System
### Block Diagram
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[Ultrasonic/Pressure Sensors] --> M[Microcontroller]
    M --> L[LoRa/GSM Module]
    L --> P[Cloud Platform]
    P --> A[Mobile/Web App]
    A --> U[User Alerts]
    M --> K[Pump Controller]
```

### Flowchart
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Read water level]
    B --> C{Below minimum?}
    C -- Yes --> D[Trigger pump ON]
    D --> F[Log event and notify]
    C -- No --> E{Above maximum?}
    E -- Yes --> G[Trigger pump OFF]
    G --> F
    E -- No --> H[Maintain state]
    F --> B
    H --> B
```

